# Release evidence gate

Apply this rule automatically whenever an agent plans, prepares, approves, or
publishes a source release. The developer must not need to invoke this rule by
name.

Before describing a release as ready, read `policy/release-evidence.yml`. Use its
path classifications to select every required verification command for the files
changed since the previous release, and require each selected command to pass.

If `policy/release-evidence.yml` is absent, unreadable, or does not classify an
affected path, stop the release-readiness decision. Name the missing policy
context and leave suitability unresolved. Do not infer checks from other
projects, silently skip unclassified paths, or weaken automatic application into
an on-demand review.

Only a human maintainer can approve an exception or authorize publication.
